course: dictionary
lesson: 3625
title: Finches and their beaks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A finch is a small songbird. Its beak is short, strong and cone-shaped, which is good for cracking open seeds. Context helps you see this: «Darwin's finches have beaks suited to seeds, insects or cactus.» Suited means fitting well, so a beak suited to seeds is one that works well for eating seeds.
explain: Context also tells you why beaks differ. «Birds whose beaks fitted the food survived better, so beaks changed.» The words survived better and changed show that the birds with the right beak lived longer and had young, so over many generations the beaks slowly changed.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. A thick beak for seeds and a thin beak for insects both make sense, so you have understood the word finch and its beak correctly.
fact: A finch is a small songbird with a short, strong, cone-shaped beak for cracking seeds.
fact: Goldfinches, chaffinches and greenfinches are all kinds of finch.
fact: «Canaries» are small finches, and long ago coal miners carried them underground to warn of bad gas.
fact: Darwin's finches on the Galápagos Islands have beaks suited to their food, and they helped Charles Darwin develop his ideas.
fact: A group of goldfinches is called «a charm of finches».
exercise: «Darwin's finches have beaks suited to seeds, insects or cactus.» What does suited mean? | Lost | Stuck together | *Fitting well | Painted
exercise: What is a finch? | A type of tree | A kind of fish | A large bird that cannot fly | *A small songbird with a short, strong beak
exercise: Which phrase names a group of goldfinches? | *A charm of finches | A pride of lions | A herd of cows | A flock of geese
test: What is the beak of a finch that eats seeds like? | Soft and bendy like a worm | Long and curved for catching fish | *Short, strong and cone-shaped for cracking seeds | Thin and pointed for sipping nectar
test: Why did the beaks of Darwin's finches change over many generations? | Because the birds wanted new colours | Because people painted their beaks | *Because birds whose beaks fitted their food survived better | Because the islands got much colder
exam: Which of these is a canary? | A large black crow | A kind of bat | *A small finch whose males are famous for their songs | A fish that swims in ponds
